---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Tomfoolery"
  description="A little about Tom."
  image="/images/social/about.png"
  imageAlt="About Tom — work, coffee, collections, and learning in public."
>
  <article class="editorial-page editorial-about">
    <header class="editorial-page-lead editorial-about__lead">
      <div>
        <span class="editorial-kicker">About Tom</span>
        <h1>A little about me.</h1>
      </div>
      <p>Work, coffee, collections, and a habit of learning by making things.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="editorial-about__body">
      <figure class="editorial-about__portrait">
        <div class="editorial-photo-mat">
          <img
            src="/images/about-tom.webp"
            srcset="/images/about-tom-480.webp 480w, /images/about-tom.webp 768w"
            sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 36vw, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
            width="768"
            height="1024"
            alt="Tom standing outdoors in warm evening light, wearing a suit and tie."
            class="block h-auto w-full"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <div class="editorial-about__prose">
        <p>
          Most days, I work from home for a medical supply company. I handle
          revenue cycle work, mainly Medicare and Humana billing and
          collections, using FinThrive. There is a lot of detail to keep
          straight, but I enjoy taking a messy problem and finding a clear way
          through it.
        </p>
        <p>
          One of my biggest goals is to become a better supervisor. I want to
          communicate clearly, help people do their best work, and stay
          organized enough that I am not adding chaos to anyone else's day. I am
          also trying to build better routines for my own time, because that is
          still a work in progress.
        </p>
        <p>
          I have always been the person who wants to try the newest piece of
          technology and understand how it works. Lately that has meant spending
          a lot of time with LLMs, AI, automation, and small hands on projects.
          I am less interested in the hype than I am in finding out what these
          tools can actually make easier.
        </p>
        <p>
          When I am not working or tinkering with something, I am usually taking
          care of Scout, my fourteen year old dog, and Theo, my new cat. I love
          making coffee and collecting Pokémon cards. I also love to bake,
          although I have not made enough time for it lately. I would like to
          get back to it.
        </p>
        <p class="editorial-about__pullquote">
          This site is a place for all of it. The things I am learning, the
          things I collect, and the projects I keep convincing myself to start.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
